      "title": "I didn't reverse-engineer the protocol for my blood pressure monitor in 24 hours",
      "url": "https://james.belchamber.com/articles/blood-pressure-monitor-reverse-engineering/",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "date": "2025-11-11T21:25:19Z",
      "language": "en",
      "section": "us_news",
      "raw_content": "Yesterday after receiving my yearly flu vaccine at the pharmacy I was offered a blood pressure test, which reported a reading that made the young pharmacist who had just given me my vaccine a bit worried. Off the back of this she offered me a 24 hour study, and then strapped a cuff to my arm plumbed into a little device which I had to wear in a little caddy - the cuff would inflate every 30 minutes during the day and every 60 minutes during the night, and then tomorrow I would bring it back for analysis.",
      "organization": "",
      "arxiv_id": "",
      "link_verified": true,
      "focus_match": [],
      "priority_hint": 0
