      "raw_content": "iPod Socks are a set of multi-colored cotton knit socks introduced by Apple Inc. in November 2004 for protection of iPods from damage during travel. [ 1 ] On October 26, 2004, Apple CEO Steve Jobs jokingly presented the socks as a \"revolutionary new product\" at a special music event . [ 2 ] [ 3 ] They were available in a package of six different colors, including green , purple , grey , blue , orange , and pink , for US$ 29 ( equivalent to $49 in 2025 ), or about US$5 a sock ( equivalent to $9 in 2025 ). [ 4 ] [ 5 ]",
